   1: #!/bin/bash
   2: # GATE 13 -- PowerPC single-precision conversion fidelity, on real guest instructions.
   3: #
   4: # What this protects
   5: # -----------------
   6: # #304 gave `frsp` the rounding mode it never read (the narrowing was a host C cast,
   7: # nearest-always, so the three directed modes were unreachable) and taught `stfs` the
   8: # ISA's denormalization band, which it had been flushing to signed zero. #305 stopped
   9: # `lfs`/`stfs` from destroying a NaN's sign and payload: the value-domain transport
  10: # (interpret -> host double -> store) structurally cannot carry them, so the NaN classes
  11: # are handled by bit surgery on the pattern instead.
  12: #
  13: # Why this gate had to exist BEFORE the fixes
  14: # ------------------------------------------
  15: # There is no PowerPC OS rig -- no guest boots on this path -- so the defects were found
  16: # by a cold-debugger spike and every one of them could only be believed once an
  17: # instrument measured it. The rows below were run against the COMMITTED build first and
  18: # their committed bytes recorded; the fix then had to flip exactly the DISC rows and
  19: # leave every PIN untouched. That baseline sweep is what makes "the fix worked" a
  20: # measurement rather than a claim, and it caught three of the author's own wrong
  21: # predictions before any code changed (frsp's RN overflow to Infinity is ISA-correct,
  22: # and the negative band row keeps its sign through the flush).
  23: #
  24: # Three row classes, and why PINs are not decoration
  25: # -------------------------------------------------
  26: #   PIN  -- correct today, must stay. Includes two POLICY pins: for finite values at
  27: #           and above ~2^129 the letter of Book I would splice-WRAP the exponent, and
  28: #           this fork deliberately keeps #287's +/-Inf instead (the letter turns a
  29: #           finite overflow into a NaN pattern: 1.5*2^128 -> 0x7FC00000). A policy pin
  30: #           failing means someone changed a known divergence without updating the
  31: #           record -- worth knowing either way.
  32: #   DISC -- discriminator: committed byte is the defect, want flips with the fix.
  33: #   DIV  -- known divergence left to a later round, pinned so it cannot drift.
  34: #   [#556, 2026-10-02 -- a records correction; the text above is kept as it was written] The DISC classification
  35: #   includes 7 negative controls in CAUSE_ROWS that verify non-raising of exception flags (yielding identical values
  36: #   before and after #330), contrary to :32 defining DISC as values that flip with the fix.  (hbundle_regress27:F11:
  37: #   regress/artifacts/astraretro_harness_20260926/HARNESS_DISPOSITIONS.md)
  38: #
  39: # #310's eighteen rows cover the eight float UPDATE forms, every one of which
  40: # stopped the emulator before this round -- neither the primary opcodes
  41: # 0x31/0x33/0x35/0x37 nor the indexed 567/631/695/759 were defined or decoded.
  42: # Each form gets BOTH halves of its contract: a value row and a base-register
  43: # row. A diff-review seat caught the first version giving five forms a base row
  44: # only, which would have passed an implementation with the wrong transfer size
  45: # that still advanced the base.
  46: #
  47: # The two non-update rows assert the mirror image, that the base is UNCHANGED --
  48: # and their displacement and index are NONZERO on purpose. With a zero offset
  49: # the effective address equals the base, so a wrongly-updating implementation
  50: # would write back exactly the value the row expects: the same seat found both
  51: # controls vacuous that way.
  52: #
  53: # The control row is load-bearing: `msr=0x2000` must take or every FP instruction
  54: # raises FPU-unavailable and the probe measures nothing. A dead probe SKIPs; it never
  55: # passes quietly. The mode rows additionally read FPSCR back, because a mode that
  56: # silently failed to take would turn every directed-mode row into a second copy of
  57: # the RN row.
  58: # [#556, 2026-10-02 -- a records correction; the text above is kept as it was written] Absence of PPC_CONV_RESULT=
  59: # invokes gate_skip, preserving earlier failures. With a result present, missing control or mode-readback tokens
  60: # fail; PPC_CONV_CONTROL=DEAD also fails. FPSCR writes are verified in four separate sessions, once per rounding
  61: # mode.  (hbundle_regress27:F12: regress/artifacts/astraretro_harness_20260926/HARNESS_DISPOSITIONS.md)
  62: #
  63: # Those rows set FPSCR by DEBUGGER WRITE rather than through the guest's own `mtfsf`,
  64: # which used to be necessary: #324 found that instruction building its write mask with
  65: # an eight-bit stride across four-bit fields, so half the FM bits wrote nothing and the
  66: # rest wrote the wrong fields. It is fixed and has six rows of its own now. The
  67: # debugger write stays because it keeps the mode rows independent of a second
  68: # instruction's correctness -- which is the property that let #324 be found at all.
  69: #
  70: # The `mtfsf` rows used to record a DIVERGENCE here: FM=0x80 selects field 0, whose bits
  71: # 1 and 2 are FEX and VX, and mtfsf copied them straight out of frB although Book I
  72: # lists it among the five instructions that "cannot alter FPSCR FEX / VX explicitly".
  73: # #327 closed that, and the row now expects hardware's 90000000 instead of the
  74: # emulator's old f0000000. THREE MORE ROWS MOVED WITH IT, because VX and FEX are
  75: # DERIVED and the recompute re-establishes them from whatever mtfsf did write: FM=0x40
  76: # gains VX from VXSNAN, FM=0x0f gains both from VXSOFT/VXSQRT/VXCVI plus VE, and
  77: # `mtfsf clears` keeps both because its preloaded causes and enables survive the
  78: # field-0 write. FM=0xff is unchanged only by coincidence -- with every cause and
  79: # enable set, derivation reproduces the copy -- and FM=0x01 selects a field with no
  80: # causes in it at all.
  81: #
  82: # All four bytes were PRE-REGISTERED from Book I before the code was written, which is
  83: # what makes this gate the fix's acceptance test rather than a transcript of it.
  84: # FM=0x40 stays the clean companion row for field PLACEMENT: it holds VXSNAN, which
  85: # the guest could not clear at all until #324 (its nibble landed above bit 31).
  86: #
  87: # #325's `fctiwz` rows carry a warning of their own. That row was pinned as a known
  88: # DIVERGENCE from #304 onward with its answer recorded as 00000000 -- and it was never
  89: # measuring the instruction it named: its word had frB = 0, so it converted f0 while
  90: # the probe seeded f1, and the zero came from an empty register. The `fctiwz 1.0
  91: # control` row exists because of it: a wrong register field yields zero for ANY
  92: # operand, so rows expecting 0x80000000 or 0 can be satisfied by accident and a row
  93: # expecting 1 cannot.
  94: set -u
