51:         rA <- r & m
52: and the prose at :29737 -- "A mask is generated having 1 bits from bit MB through
53: bit 63 and 0 bits elsewhere.  The rotated data is ANDed with the generated mask".
54: IBM bit numbering is big-endian, so MASK(b,63) is the LOW (64-b) bits: for b=32
55: that is 0x00000000ffffffff, which is why `rldicl rA,rS,0,32' is the canonical
56: 32-bit zero-extend (`clrldi rA,rS,32', manual :29758).
57: EVERY `want' in this probe is computed from those five lines, never from the tree.
