60: decoder and executed by the real handler, on the UNMODIFIED in-tree `-E bareppc'.
61: No machine description edited, no device_add, no CPU model override -- bareppc's
62: own MACHINE_DEFAULT_CPU is PPC970, which is 64-bit in the in-tree CPU table, and
63: 64-bit is what the decoder requires (`if (cpu->cd.ppc.bits == 32) goto bad').
64: 
65: THE ORACLE is a guest-visible wrong VALUE, not a process death, so it is read
66: directly out of the destination register.  Five controls (this said `Four' until #565; NL6):
67:   live          `li r9,0x1234' in the same session reads back 0x1234 -- the guest
68:                 really executes and the readback path really works.
69:   seed holds    a destination register seeded with a sentinel and then stepped
70:                 over a NON-WRITING instruction still holds the sentinel.  This is
